  "term": "clinical risk assessment",
  "definition": "Clinical risk assessment is the process of estimating a patient’s chance of harmful health outcomes by reviewing clinical risk factors, often with a scoring system. In the source, it refers to using risk scores and sometimes biomarkers to improve individualized prediction when treatment decisions are uncertain.",
